U.S. Biological Product Development and Regulatory Approval Process
Our allogeneic therapeutic candidates will be regulated in the United States as biological products. The process required by the FDA before a biological product may be tested and
marketed in the United States generally involves the following:
• completion of nonclinical laboratory tests and animal studies according to good laboratory practices, or GLP, regulations and applicable requirements for the
humane use of laboratory animals or other applicable regulations;
• submission to the FDA of an IND application, which must become effective before human clinical trials may begin and must be updated annually or when
significant changes are made;
• approval by an independent Institutional Review Board, or IRB, or ethics committee at each clinical site before the trial begins;
